Z||000003||danny boy||07-18-2001||12:35 AM||||Five point harnesses are a big pain. don't get em for a street car. My non stock seats and stock belts work fine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Fieromaster||07-18-2001||12:55 AM||||not a 5 point but a 4 point.. dont want a crotch belt.. then id have to cut my seat up<P>------------------<BR>      <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">        <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||07-18-2001||08:31 AM||||if you look at the top of my seats you'll see the holes in it.. if you just loop the belts around the stock seats in the event your in an accident and the harness isn't above or level with you shoulders you'll compress your spine and cause more damage than you would've with stock belts. the crotch strap isn't needed but the top ones need to be in the proper place or you'll be fighting with them everytime you get in/out of the car.. they won't stay up and they are uncomfy...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wannabe||07-18-2001||11:20 AM||||I have a racing harness with the stock seat. You don;t want to do this unless you have VERY broad shoulders. It's better than the factory seabels for track work, but I only did it because I couldn't get a proper seat in time.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||07-18-2001||11:31 AM||||Trav.... how do you find the Corbeau's for the street?? I would like to get a set of sparco's this winter, I run 4 point pyrotecs with stock seats right now , there no good with stock seats I wouldn't bother. For the track I use the stock belt. I mounted mine to the ledge onthe window , used hi grade bolts.<P><BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
